"Refinements landed (commit 9322a5b) after user review: (1) VERIFICATION CODE -- request_login(account_name, verification_code); the code is chosen by the requesting device, displayed only on its screen, and stored in login_request_codes, a PRIVATE server-only table (no client can read it; voters must obtain it out-of-band from the requesting device's screen, so approval proves coordination, not a blind click). respond_login split into accept_login_request(id, code) -- mismatch = Err, approval does not count, no response row recorded (txn rollback) -- and refuse_login_request(id), no code required (refusing an intruder stays the easy path). UI: requester generates+displays a 6-digit code; approver prompt has a code input; e2e covers mismatch (stays Pending, zero responses) and matched accept. (2) NORMALIZED JOIN confirmed already in place: account_identities is identity(PK) -> account_id (btree) -- no arrays anywhere -- and player_controller_components has unique account_id, so identity -> account -> player controller is two O(1) index steps; a future observer component gets the same unique-account_id treatment. Full gate green (cargo, clippy, web check, 101 unit, e2e 0-6)."